5.1.0 (all 3 regions) | unhealthy (release marked \"degraded\") | 18% | v5.0.0 |\n| `payments-worker` | v3.4.0 (all 3 regions) | unhealthy (release marked \"unhealthy\") | 18% | v3.3.0 |\n\nBoth have the same error rate, and both have one bad release on top of a healthy one. The release history doesn't show timestamps, so I can't tell which was deployed this morning. One service's errors may also be causing the other's.\n\nRolling back production and paging on-call are real actions, so I'd rather not guess. Which do you want?\n\n1. **Roll back only `payments-api`** to v5.0.0\n2. **Roll back only `payments-worker`** to v3.3.0\n3. **Roll back both** to their last healthy versions\n\nI can also open the SEV2 for one service or both. Both rollback targets were healthy in production, so neither needs change-manager approval. Once you confirm, I'll do it straight away.", "type": "text"}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01RNxQ7edBBaepkxavyb5Bt4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01KHhj7LS4aWrZh5VCoDAHwS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-worker errors after v3.4.0 deploy", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "payments-worker v3.4.0 (deployed this morning) unhealthy in all prod regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with ~18% error rate. payments-api (v5.1.0) also showing 18% errors, believed downstream of the worker. Rolling payments-worker back to last healthy release v3.3.0.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2", "confidence": 0.92}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01E5jCcxERL8K1DHJrsuVchB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "too